From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri.3012@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] b43: add AC-PHY support for the BCM4352/BCM4360 family

The AC-PHY / radio 2069 port of https://github.com/aleferri/b43-ac-wip
at bb6a455 (b43/ directory), merged onto backports 7.2 and OpenWrt's
810-815 b43 patches with a three-way merge against v6.8 b43:

- keep the backports Kconfig dependencies (depends on m, FW_LOADER,
  CORDIC, SSB_*) and CPTCFG_ symbol names
- keep the upstream changes since v6.8: emulated chanctx ops,
  op_config radio_idx, op_stop suspend, ieee80211_radar_detected()
  chanctx argument, linux/unaligned.h, core rev 0x16, allhwsupport
- keep OpenWrt's gpiomask parameter, no-PIO fallback and antenna
  control in the code the port moved

Index: backports-7.2/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/Kconfig
===================================================================
--- backports-7.2.orig/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/Kconfig
+++ backports-7.2/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/Kconfig
@@ -150,13 +150,29 @@ config B43_PHY_LCN
 	  Say N, this is BROKEN and crashes driver.
 
 config B43_PHY_AC
-	bool "Support for AC-PHY (802.11ac) devices (BROKEN)"
-	depends on B43 && B43_BCMA && BROKEN
+	bool "Support for AC-PHY (802.11ac) devices"
+	depends on B43 && B43_BCMA
 	help
 	  This PHY type can be found in the following chipsets:
 	  PCI: BCM4352, BCM4360
 
-	  Say N, this is BROKEN and crashes driver.
+	  Support is experimental.
+
+	  If unsure, say N.
+
+config B43_DFS
+	bool "Radar channels in AP mode on the AC-PHY"
+	depends on B43_PHY_AC && CFG80211_CERTIFICATION_ONUS
+	help
+	  Let an access point run on channels that require radar detection.
+	  mac80211 runs the channel availability check and the AC-PHY polls
+	  its radar pulse FIFOs. A radar is reported when more pulses arrive
+	  within 100 ms than the stock driver lets pass as noise: the pulses
+	  are counted, not matched against the radar patterns, which
+	  certification requires, and bursts of fewer than 17 pulses go
+	  unseen.
+
+	  Say N.
 
 # This config option automatically enables b43 LEDS support,
 # if it's possible.
